      paragraphs: [
        `Selling online is where licence type produces the largest difference in how a site is actually built, and where most of the mistakes we see live.`,
        `A mainland company with ecommerce activity on its licence sells and ships inside the UAE market with the fewest moving parts. Its store can complete sales, quote delivery across the emirates subject only to courier capability, and invoice the customer from the same entity the customer saw on the site.`,
        `A free zone company's store depends on its fulfilment route. If goods are held in the zone and sold to mainland consumers, the customs step described earlier exists and has to be designed around. If fulfilment runs through a mainland entity or distributor, the store needs to be clear about who sells, who invoices and who handles returns. Some zones are built specifically for this trade — Dubai CommerCity, for example, is a free zone established for ecommerce operations — and the clustering exists precisely because the logistics need thinking about. Which arrangement is available to you is a question for your zone, not for us.`,
        `Three build-level consequences follow. The checkout: whether it completes a sale or captures an order for fulfilment elsewhere. The delivery options: honest zones with honest promises, reflecting the actual route rather than a national flat rate. And the paperwork: the invoice must come from the entity that sold the goods, with the right TRN, and the returns address must be somewhere a parcel can actually be received. Getting these three right is most of what separates a UAE store that runs quietly from one that generates disputes.`,
        `Marketplaces add their own layer. Platforms onboarding UAE sellers ask for licence documents and will assess whether your activity covers what you intend to list. Doing that check before you build your own store tells you something useful about how your licence is read in practice. And whatever you sell on a marketplace, your own site is the asset you own — the balance between the two is covered on <a href='/uae/ecommerce-website-development/'>ecommerce website development</a>.`,
      ],
